version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Wendinkonte/realistic-well-log-imputation-benchmark
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and reproducibility package for a benchmark of eleven
  well-log imputation methods, plus seventeen baselines and controls, across five
  missingness regimes (single, block, profile, the synthetic multi-log blackout and an
  empirical blackout drawn from the observed gaps), evaluated under a leakage-controlled
  leave-one-well-out protocol on 18 Paris Basin geothermal wells (19 in release 1.0; the
  depth-step QC of release 1.1.0 excludes one well). The package contains the data
  pipeline with depth-step QC, the masking generators, tabular, sequential and spatial
  graph imputers with their baselines and controls, the evaluation harness with
  fold-local scaling and identical evaluation masks across methods, per-log metrics,
  well-level significance tests (Friedman, exact Wilcoxon with Holm correction, by-well
  bootstrap) and the leakage experiments. The well-log data themselves are proprietary
  and are not redistributed; the derived statistics, including anonymised per-well
  sufficient statistics from which every table of the revised article can be recomputed,
  are released.
keywords:
  - well-log imputation
  - missing data
  - partial blackout
  - missing not at random
  - data leakage
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
  - baselines
  - graph neural networks
  - geothermal
  - Paris Basin
